body:
The previous Word RAM archive registration used a standalone `VERIFY.json` as if it were a generic registered research package. Its `inputs` entry was not repository-relative, so the shared planner failed before any selected package replay; changing only that path would then make the generic validator reject this legacy package's non-generic schema.

This maintenance PR preserves the standalone capsule and removes the accidental generic registration:

- rename `VERIFY.json` byte-identically to `STANDALONE-VERIFY.json`;
- update only the standalone `MANIFEST.json` inventory key and its README descriptor reference;
- keep every mathematical source, data file, result, license and attribution byte unchanged;
- leave the shared planner and generic schema gates unchanged.

Validation from the exact current main base `df0137efd35e11b4445734bf612bdd4c7ebc330c`:

- the original current package fails its own integrity check exactly at the stale `VERIFY.json` inventory entry;
- the repaired standalone verifier passes its complete normal replay in 7.6 seconds (8 NTT tests, 65,537 RAM slices, 5,096 butterfly cases and 277 whole-program cases);
- its intentional Python `-O` rejection remains intact;
- all 32 manifest hashes pass after replay;
- the actual planner selects no generic package for this metadata-only change, while shared-control planning completes with 3,353 registered packages and excludes the legacy Word RAM capsule;
- `scripts/research_package.py --changed-since HEAD^ --explain-plan ...` returns an empty replay matrix.

This corrects CI registration metadata only. It does not claim a new κ, scientific admission, or a complete multiplication theorem.
